# Claude Installation & Setup Guide (English)

[한국어 가이드](./claude.ko.md) · [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest)

You do not need terminal knowledge. In the **Claude desktop app**, a few mouse clicks and one pasted prompt connect the Claire Bible `claire` plugin to your Claire Bible server. Then you can save and extract URLs and documents and search your knowledge graph.

---

## Where Does It Work?

| Claude surface | What you can do | Where to start |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Code mode (`</>`) of the Claude desktop app**, Claude Code in a terminal | Save, extract, and search (`/claire:ingest`, `/claire:query`) | Steps 1 to 3 below |
| claude.ai web, normal chat of the desktop app, mobile app | Search (read) only | [Read-only connection](#readonly-connector) at the end |

---

## Before You Start (1 Minute)

1. Sign in to your **Claire Bible web page**.
2. In **LLM provider settings** (`/account/providers`), switch **Extraction mode** to **`Agent Client (client)`**.
3. Keep **MCP Settings** (`/account/mcp`) open. You copy the **Claude quick setup prompt** from this page.

---

## Step 1: Install the Plugin (Mouse Clicks Only)

1. Open the **Claude desktop app** and select the **`</>`** icon (Code mode) at the top of the window.
2. Click **`Plugins`** in the left menu.
3. Click **`Add`** at the top right and open the **`Add marketplace`** dialog.
4. Paste this text into the **URL** field and click **`Sync`**.
   ```text
   {{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}
   ```
   - The notice *"Only add marketplaces you trust"* is normal. This is the official Claire Bible repository, and it contains no server passwords or tokens.
5. Next to the **Claire Bible** (`claire`) plugin in the list, click **`Add to this computer`**.

---

## Step 2: Connect Your Claire Bible Server (Paste One Prompt)

1. On the Claire Bible **`/account/mcp`** page, in the **Official Agent Marketplace (GitHub)** card, click **Copy** next to the **`Claude quick setup prompt`**.
   - To start from GitHub, copy this prompt and replace only `<your-claire-server>` with the address of your server:
   ```text
   Set up Claire Bible on this computer. Run these commands in order, one at a time,
   and tell me each result.
   1) claude plugin install claire --marketplace {{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}
   2) claude mcp add --transport http --scope user claire https://<your-claire-server>/mcp
   3) claude mcp login claire
   If a step says that it is already done, continue with the next step.
   If the claude command is not found, stop and tell me.
   Do not change other settings. At the end, tell me to restart Claude.
   ```
2. Click **`+ New`** at the top left of the Claude app, paste the prompt, and send it.
   - *Permission to run commands*: when Claude asks if it can run these commands, select **Allow**. All three commands change only the Claire Bible setup.
3. **Claire Bible sign-in (OAuth 2.1)**: command 3 opens your browser. Sign in to Claire Bible and approve the **`readonly`** and **`write`** scopes.
4. Quit the Claude app fully and open it again.

---

## Step 3: Make Sure It Works

1. In the left menu, open **`Plugins`** and make sure that **Claire Bible** (`claire`) is shown.
2. Open a new conversation with **`+ New`** and send this line:
   ```text
   /claire:query Show the list of my knowledge bases
   ```
3. When the answer shows the names and document counts of your knowledge bases, the connection is complete.

---

## Commands Ready to Use (`v{{VERSION}}`)

- **`/claire:ingest <url, file, or note>`** (or **`/claire:ingest`** with no arguments):
  - Saves a web address, a local file (PDF, DOCX, ODT, MD, TXT, RST, ADOC, HTML), or a text note on your server and completes extraction in one step.
  - When run with no arguments (`/claire:ingest`) or asked to process waiting items, drains `pending` items staged from the Web UI, Telegram, or feeds.
  - Invokes the hidden forked subagent runner (`extract-runner` -> `claire:extractor`) automatically, so you only need to learn two commands.
- **`/claire:query <question>`**:
  - Finds entities, relations, and documents in your personal knowledge base and in shared knowledge bases.

Examples (URL ingest, file/note ingest, empty-argument pending queue drain, graph query):

```text
/claire:ingest https://example.com/article
/claire:ingest ./notes/spec.pdf
/claire:ingest
/claire:query Find documents about Fedify
```

### Safety Controls

- Only the **isolated extraction agent** (`claire:extractor`) reads a staged source. It has only Claire Bible MCP tools and cannot use files, a shell, or a browser.
- `/claire:ingest` invokes the hidden forked subagent runner automatically, so users only learn `/claire:ingest` and `/claire:query`.
- If Claude on the main thread tries to read a raw staged source directly, the `PreToolUse` guard hook (`hooks/hooks.json`) stops the call and directs you to `/claire:ingest`:
  `"extract_read is allowed only in the claire:extractor subagent. Use /claire:ingest, or give the document_id to claire:extractor."`
- Contributing a document to a shared knowledge base always asks for your confirmation first.

---

## Update or Remove the Plugin

1. In the left menu, open **`Plugins`** and open the **`Manage marketplaces`** dialog.
2. Click **`…`** next to **`claire-agents`** to update or remove it. (When you remove the marketplace, the `claire` plugin is removed too.)
3. Start the Claude app again after an update.

---

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Solution |
| :--- | :--- |
| `/claire:query` or another command answers that it *cannot find the tools* | Do Step 2 again. The server must be registered with the name **`claire`**. A server that you add as a Claude **connector** has a different name, and the plugin cannot use it. |
| It works in one folder but not in a different folder | The server is registered for that folder only. Run the Step 2 prompt (it has `--scope user`) again. |
| Claude answers that the *claude command is not found* | Ask Claude *"Tell me how to install the Claude Code command-line tool"*, install it, and do Step 2 again. |
| You missed the browser sign-in window | In a new conversation, send *"Run the command claude mcp login claire"*. |
| You signed in, but the answer says that there is no `write` scope | You cleared **Allow write access** on the approval page. Sign in again as above and keep the box selected. |
| A new version does not apply | Update `claire-agents` in **`Manage marketplaces`**, and start the app again. |

